extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 92 (cache p093; text layer, page_offset +1), read against a render of both columns. The whole entry, lore through cybernetics, is on printed 92: the stat block runs down the left column and ends at the Cybernetics paragraph in the right column, above the Robot Pilot heading, so source_book is p.92. The book heads it Infantryman O.C.C.; the class_id is republic-infantryman and the name Republic Infantryman to tell it from the NGR Infantry Soldier. || GROUP: men-of-arms, men_of_arms: true. The book''s class list (printed 78) files it as Military: Infantryman O.C.C. under Republic of Japan & Mercenaries, and High-Tech O.C.C.s. No S.D.C. or hit points are printed, so the core values apply. || XP: the Cyberoid, Republic Infantrymen column, top right of the Experience Point Tables page (cache p217, folio 216), read off a render: 0 / 1,951 / 3,901 / 8,801 / 17,601 / 35,601 / 50,601 / 70,601 / 95,601 / 125,601 / 175,601 / 225,601 / 275,601 / 325,601 / 375,601. The book prints level 8 as 70,600-95,600, the previous band''s upper bound, so 70,601 is stored. || ATTRIBUTES: P.E. 9; a high P.S. and P.P. are suggested but not required, so only P.E. is stored. || SKILLS: Basic Mathematics is Mathematics: Basic 45+10; Language: Japanese & American (+20%) is Language: Native Tongue for Japanese at the catalog''s 98% cap and Language: Other for American as a one-pick choice at +20; Literacy: Japanese & American (+20%) is Literacy: Native Language 40+20 and Literacy: Other as a one-pick choice at +20 (the catalog has no Japanese or American rows); Computer Operation 40+10; Radio: Basic 45+10; Pilot Tanks & APCs is Military: Tanks & APCs 36+10; Read Sensory Equipment is the Sensory Equipment row 30+10 (the book''s own skill list, printed 187-188, prints it as Radar/Sonar Operations (Read Sensor Equipment), 30% +5%, the same figures); Weapon Systems 40+10; Running; W.P. Energy Rifle and W.P. Energy Pistol; W.P.: one of choice is a one-pick choice from Weapon Proficiencies. || HAND TO HAND: Expert; martial arts/Judo, or Assassin if evil, for one related pick; Jujitsu for two at the GM''s discretion. Martial arts/Judo is stored as Hand to Hand: Basic Martial Arts/Judo, which the book describes (printed 193) as equivalent to Judo and the basic hand to hand of the Republic''s armed forces and police. || RELATED: seven, plus two skills and a W.P. at level 3, two at level 6, and one at levels 9, 12 and 14. A schedule entry carries a count and no category, so the level-3 grant is stored as three picks from the class''s related categories, with the W.P. requirement in the note. Espionage: Wilderness Survival only is the Wilderness row of that name, which the class also grants; Mechanical: Automotive only is Automotive Mechanics. Electrical and Science: none, so they are not offered. || SECONDARY: six from the same list without bonuses. || MONEY: one month''s salary, 1800 credits; room and board are free. || EQUIPMENT: Trooper or Marine armor is a choice of the AT-A14 Trooper and AT-A15 Marine rows. The energy rifle and pistol are choices led by the typical AT-88 and A-30 (the AT-30 Combat Laser Pistol row), with this book''s other ArmaTech and H-Brand energy weapons offered. The armed forces personal backpack is the PR-1 standard backpack (printed 116). Parade uniform is the dress uniform row. || CYBERNETICS: 60% start with four implants of choice, no bionics; a percentage chance cannot be stored, so it is in restrictions and not modelled."
