## Lore

The infantry are the Republic of Japan''s ground pounders, the men and women who stand between the Republic and its many enemies. Most of them, about four in five, are citizens of Hiroshima, Kure and Iwakuni: survivors of the Great Cataclysm who are willing to die to defend their land.

The rest are volunteers too, usually peasant refugees who came to the newly arrived cities once they were convinced the newcomers were neither monsters nor invaders. These peasant-soldiers have all been taught basic literacy and computer use, and they are if anything more driven than their comrades, because they have seen what waits for the prosperous cities if the soldiers fail.

The infantry resent the glory heaped on robot and power armor pilots, who fight behind inches of M.D.C. armor while the foot soldier takes the greatest risks. Brawls at military bars on leave are common enough that there are infantry-only bars and pilot-only bars, and one group does not walk into the other''s unless it is looking for a fight.

## GM Notes

Additional equipment may be issued in special combat situations.

Cybernetics: 60% of infantrymen start with four cybernetic implants of choice (no bionics). They are unlikely to receive any others, except as medical and prosthetic replacements, until they leave the service. Roll or assign this at creation and record the implants by hand.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'republic-infantryman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'republic-infantryman';

